    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88">

                <pb facs="0116" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/1136: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-07T14:00:00+09:00">June 7, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 7—6:08 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>151. 1. In my initial interview today with the new Foreign Minister,<anchor
                        n="22" xml:id="d88-f1"/> Hirota asked me to tell the President and yourself
                    that his <pb facs="0117" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/> guiding policy in conducting
                    Japan’s relations with the United States would be based on the exchange of
                    messages with you in 1934.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d88-f2"/></p>
                <p>2. With regard to the Sino-Japanese affairs he said that his former “three
                    points” were too abstract for present circumstances. He therefore proposed to
                    find concrete solutions of the various outstanding problems between Japan and
                    China.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d88-f1" n="22" xml:id="d88-f1-content">
                <p>Koki Hirota returned to this post in the Cabinet of Prince Fumimaro Konoye on
                    June 4.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d88-f2" n="23" xml:id="d88-f2-content">
                <p>Exchanged on February 21 and March 3, 1934, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_127"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol.
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 127</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_129">129</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
